From 86f84c85510ee802ac365bfeb1036b66aa321a93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:56:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: skip NPU TXD allocation without offload

CONFIG_MT76_NPU can be enabled even when mt76_npu_init() fails to find
an Airoha provider and the PCI driver continues without offload. Moving
the TXD buffer allocations out of __mt7996_npu_hw_init() put them before
its NULL-provider check. The fallback path now reserves six unused
coherent buffers and can fail ordinary Wi-Fi probe with -ENOMEM.

Check whether offload is active before allocating the NPU-only buffers,
matching the existing NPU RX queue initialization guard.

Fixes: e826923c533a ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: Store DMA mapped buffer addresses in mt7996_npu_hw_init()")
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/npu.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7996/npu.c b/mt7996/npu.c
index 23142e1..f24d295 100644
--- a/mt7996/npu.c
+++ b/mt7996/npu.c
@@ -609,6 +609,9 @@ int mt7996_npu_hw_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 {
 	int i, err;
 
+	if (!mt76_npu_device_active(&dev->mt76))
+		return 0;
+
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(ARRAY_SIZE(dev->npu_txd_addr) % 3);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->npu_txd_addr); i += 3) {
-- 
2.43.0

